<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<title>PostoQue — One queue for every brand, every channel</title>
<meta name="description" content="PostoQue is a self-hosted content operations engine — plan, create, approve and publish across social, email and your website from one queue.">
<%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>

  <%- include('partials/header') %>

  <main class="hero wrap">
    <div class="stage">
      <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Building in public — private preview live</span>

      <h1>One queue for every<br>brand, every channel, <em>done</em>.</h1>

      <p class="lead">
        PostoQue plans, drafts and publishes your content across social, email and your own
        website — from one dashboard, one approval queue, one Claude conversation. Point it at a
        spreadsheet of raw ideas and images, and it hands back ready-to-approve posts.
      </p>

      <div class="chips">
        <div class="chip"><b>Social</b> — 9 networks</div>
        <div class="chip"><b>Email</b> — full marketing automation</div>
        <div class="chip"><b>Blog</b> — your website, drafted &amp; published</div>
        <div class="chip"><b>Claude</b> — wired into the middle of it</div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta">
        <% if (user) { %>
          <a class="btn pri" href="/dashboard">Go to dashboard</a>
        <% } else { %>
          <a class="btn pri" href="/login">Preview the product</a>
          <a class="btn gho" href="mailto:zinergeco@gmail.com?subject=PostoQue%20early%20access">Get early access</a>
        <% } %>
      </div>

      <a class="scroll-hint" href="#features">See what's inside <span>↓</span></a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <section class="features wrap" id="features">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> What's inside</span>
      <h2>One queue for everything you publish</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Nine social networks, full email marketing, and your own blog — planned, drafted and
        approved from the same dashboard, not three separate logins.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="18" cy="5" r="3"/><circle cx="6" cy="12" r="3"/><circle cx="18" cy="19" r="3"/><path d="M8.6 10.5 15.4 6.5M8.6 13.5 15.4 17.5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Social publishing</h3>
        <p>Schedule and publish across 9 networks from one shared calendar. Drag a post to reschedule it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="m3 7 9 6 9-6"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Email marketing</h3>
        <p>Campaigns, automated sequences and deliverability monitoring, sharing the same brand voice as every post.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13"/><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H18"/><path d="M8 7h7M8 10h7"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Blog &amp; website</h3>
        <p>Draft, review and publish long-form posts straight to your site — WordPress, headless CMS or a git-based build.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v3M12 18v3M3 12h3M18 12h3M5.6 5.6l2.1 2.1M16.3 16.3l2.1 2.1M5.6 18.4l2.1-2.1M16.3 7.7l2.1-2.1"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>AI drafting</h3>
        <p>Point Claude at a brief — or a spreadsheet of raw ideas and images — and get ready-to-approve variants back, per network.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 12.5 11 15l4-5.5"/><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2.5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Approval queue</h3>
        <p>Every post and every email waits for a human yes before anything goes out — designed to work from a phone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="3.2"/><circle cx="17" cy="16" r="3.2"/><path d="M11 9.5 14 14"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Multi-brand</h3>
        <p>Run unlimited brands and clients from one account, each with its own voice pack, slots and approvers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 12a8 8 0 0 1 14.5-4.6M20 12a8 8 0 0 1-14.5 4.6"/><path d="M18.5 3v4.5H14M5.5 21v-4.5H10"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Automation</h3>
        <p>Recipes that refill an empty queue, recycle top performers and escalate stale approvals — on their own.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="f-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 20V10M11 20V4M18 20v-7"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Analytics</h3>
        <p>Performance across every channel in one place, plus a weekly read written by Claude — what worked, what didn't.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="showcase wrap" id="product">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> See it in action</span>
      <h2>A real dashboard, not a mockup of one</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Screens pulled straight from the product — the same command centre, calendar and composer your team will use.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="stab" data-show="hub" aria-selected="true">Command Centre</button>
      <button class="stab" data-show="social">Social Calendar</button>
      <button class="stab" data-show="content">AI Composer</button>
    </div>

    <div class="showcase-frame">
      <div class="showcase-chrome"><span class="d red"></span><span class="d amber"></span><span class="d green"></span><span class="surl">app.postoque.com</span></div>
      <div class="showcase-imgs">
        <img class="sshot on" data-shot="hub" src="/img/screens/hubque.webp" alt="PostoQue HubQue command centre showing publishing stats, brand cover and today's schedule across five brands">
        <img class="sshot" data-shot="social" src="/img/screens/socialque.webp" alt="PostoQue SocialQue weekly calendar showing scheduled and published posts across five brands and channels">
        <img class="sshot" data-shot="content" src="/img/screens/contentque.webp" alt="PostoQue ContentQue composer showing an AI-drafted LinkedIn post with brand voice checks and a live preview">
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="showcase-cap" id="showcase-caption">Every brand, every channel, one screen — publishing status, approvals and failures at a glance.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="why wrap" id="why">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Why PostoQue</span>
      <h2>Built for the actual job, not a demo of it</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="why-grid">
      <div class="why-item">
        <div class="w-num">01</div>
        <div><h3>One queue, not five tools</h3><p>Social, email and your website blog all move through the same approval queue — not three separate logins and three separate habits to maintain.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="why-item">
        <div class="w-num">02</div>
        <div><h3>Claude does the first draft</h3><p>Point it at a spreadsheet of raw ideas or images and it hands back ready-to-approve, on-brand content — not a blank page.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="why-item">
        <div class="w-num">03</div>
        <div><h3>Approval built in, not bolted on</h3><p>Nothing publishes or sends without a human yes. It's designed mobile-first, because approval happens on a phone in a car park.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="why-item">
        <div class="w-num">04</div>
        <div><h3>Multi-brand from day one</h3><p>Manage every brand, client or workspace from one account, each with its own voice, posting slots and approvers.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="why-item">
        <div class="w-num">05</div>
        <div><h3>It never guesses on your behalf</h3><p>Auth failures, rate limits and content problems are logged and flagged — never silently retried into a platform ban.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="why-item">
        <div class="w-num">06</div>
        <div><h3>Self-hosted, your data stays yours</h3><p>Run it on your own infrastructure and own the database. No vendor lock-in, no third party sitting on your content.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta wrap">
    <div class="fc-card">
      <h2>Building in public — come see it.</h2>
      <p>Private preview is live. Ask for access, or step through the dashboard yourself.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <% if (user) { %>
          <a class="btn pri" href="/dashboard">Go to dashboard</a>
        <% } else { %>
          <a class="btn pri" href="/login">Preview the product</a>
          <a class="btn gho" href="mailto:zinergeco@gmail.com?subject=PostoQue%20early%20access">Get early access</a>
        <% } %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>

  <script>
  (function(){
    var tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.stab');
    var shots = document.querySelectorAll('.sshot');
    var caption = document.getElementById('showcase-caption');
    var surl = document.querySelector('.showcase-chrome .surl');
    var meta = {
      hub: { url: 'app.postoque.com/hub', cap: "Every brand, every channel, one screen — publishing status, approvals and failures at a glance." },
      social: { url: 'app.postoque.com/social', cap: "A shared weekly calendar across every brand and network. Drag a post to reschedule it." },
      content: { url: 'app.postoque.com/content', cap: "Claude drafts per-network variants from one brief, checked against your brand's voice before you ever see it." }
    };
    tabs.forEach(function(t){
      t.addEventListener('click', function(){
        var id = t.getAttribute('data-show');
        tabs.forEach(function(x){ x.setAttribute('aria-selected', x === t ? 'true' : 'false'); });
        shots.forEach(function(s){ s.classList.toggle('on', s.getAttribute('data-shot') === id); });
        if (meta[id]) { caption.textContent = meta[id].cap; surl.textContent = meta[id].url; }
      });
    });
  })();
  </script>

</body>
</html>
